Hello Haifei,

We can restore and recover the system state via simply mimicking the operations in time steppers. Taking the HHT stepper as example, to restore the system state at time instant T, we can do:

    ChIntegrableIIorder* mintegrable = (ChIntegrableIIorder*)hht_stepper->GetIntegrable();
    // Setup main vectors
    mintegrable->StateSetup(X, V, A);
    L.setZero(mintegrable->GetNumConstraints());
    // State at current time T
    mintegrable->StateGather(X, V, T);        // state <- system

L.setZero(mintegrable->GetNumConstraints());
    // State at current time T
    mintegrable->StateGather(X, V, T);        // state <- system
    mintegrable->StateGatherAcceleration(A);  // <- system
    mintegrable->StateGatherReactions(L);     // <- system

After one time step, or in fact at any time instant as you like, to recover the system state, you can do:

    // Scatter state -> system doing a full update
    mintegrable->StateScatter(X, V, T, true);

    // Scatter auxiliary data (A and L) -> system
    mintegrable->StateScatterAcceleration(A);
    mintegrable->StateScatterReactions(L);


Best regards,
PENG Chao


