to assign a "internal damping coefficient" to the cable element. My 
question is: how can this damping factor be interpreted? Is it similar to 
the rayleigh beta (K-proprtional) damping?

Furthermore, I think I have found a bug in: ChElementCableANCF::
ComputeInternalJacobians(double Kfactor, double Rfactor). When setting a 
damping factor using ChElementCableANCF::SetAlphaDamp() my test system 
could not be solved. Looking at the source code of  ChElementCableANCF::ComputeInternalJacobians, 
I found the following section:

