Subject: Re: [chrono] restart a simulation
From: Radu Serban
Date: Wed, 26 Feb 2020 09:24:19 +0100

Hi Lucas,

You may want to move the declarations of the state vectors *outside* the 
loop. As you have them right now, you end up scattering vectors that 
are uninitialized (so garbage). With that, your code should work as 
expected (for a system that doesn't change topology between the times 
you gather and scatter the state vectors).

On a separate note: you may want to disable the soft real-time option 
(application.SetRealtime(true)), because the mechanism used inside 
ChIrrApplication::DoStep() in that case relies on continuously adjusting 
the step size. If you want to keep enforcing soft real-time, consider 
using the alternative mechanism I implemented a while ago in 
ChRealtimeStepTimer (spinning in place until real time catches up with 
simulation time); for that however, you will need to explicitly call 
DoStepDynamics on the system:

ChRealtimeStepTimer realtime_timer;
double step_size = 0.01;
while (app->GetDevice()->run()) {
  app.BeginScene();
   app.DrawAll();
  app.EndScene();

  sys.DoStepDynamics(step_size);
  realtime_timer.Spin(step_size);
}

--Radu

