From: Radu Serban
Date: Wed, 20 Nov 2019 19:23:41 +0000

Maybe it's a write permission issue?

If you built Chrono from source, you can try to modify one of our demos and check that it works there.

At the end of the day, you can simply put the appropriate code (from ChIrrApplication.cpp) directly in your simulation loop.  This could also help you debug the issue.  Something like the following:

#include "chrono_thirdparty/filesystem/path.h"

int main() {
   // ...

    filesystem::create_directory(filesystem::path("video_capture"));
    int videoframe_num = 0;
    int videoframe_each = 1;

    while (application.GetDevice()->run()) {
        application.BeginScene();
        application.DrawAll();
        application.DoStep();

        irr::video::IImage* image = application.GetVideoDriver()->createScreenShot();
        char filename[100];
        sprintf(filename, "video_capture/screenshot%05d.bmp", (videoframe_num + 1) / videoframe_each);
        if (image)
            application.GetDevice()->getVideoDriver()->writeImageToFile(image, filename);
        image->drop();
        videoframe_num++;

        application.EndScene();
    }
}


--Radu


