Hi Nomoto,

The renderZ.pov script I provided is somewhat limited in this aspect.  In particular, to render meshes it expects an *.inp file to define a single POV-Ray object, with a particular orientation and with a name that matches the file name.

So geometry inp files generated from PoseRay need to be manually edited. Look at the end of the PoseRay-generated file hmmwv_chassis_POV_geom.inc you have and compare that with the corresponding file in the Chrono repository (under data/vehicle/hmmwv/POV-Ray).  You will see that the latter was modified to:

//Model assembly from the meshes
#declare hmmwv_chassis_POV_geom=
object{
union {
object{hmmwv_chassis_Exhaust_Pipe_  material{Exhaust_Pipe_} hollow }
object{hmmwv_chassis_Infinite_Black_  material{Infinite_Black_} hollow }
object{hmmwv_chassis_Exterior_Tan_  material{Exterior_Tan_} hollow }
object{hmmwv_chassis_Body_Drvr_Side_  material{Body_Drvr_Side_} hollow }
object{hmmwv_chassis_Interior_  material{Interior_} hollow }
object{hmmwv_chassis_PsngrSide_Door_2_  material{PsngrSide_Door_2_} hollow }
object{hmmwv_chassis_PsngrSide_Door_1_  material{PsngrSide_Door_1_} hollow }
