Subject: Re: [chrono] POV-ray positioning of geometry
From: Radu Serban
Date: Mon, 3 Jun 2019 07:11:15 +0000

Hi Mads,

The issue here is that there are two (redundant) ways to set the position of a box visualization asset.  This is something we will have to fix in order to eliminate problems such as this.

The utility functions in ChUtilsCreators (such as AddBoxGeometry) use one mechanism to set the box position and orientation, while the PovRay exporter only interprets the other...

Until we fix this issue, a workaround is to write your own function to add a box geometry which sets the position and orientation as expected by the PovRay exporter.  Something like:

void MyAddBoxGeometry(ChBody* body,
                    const ChVector<>& size,
                    const ChVector<>& pos,
                    const ChQuaternion<>& rot,
                    bool visualization) {
    body->GetCollisionModel()->AddBox(size.x(), size.y(), size.z(), pos, rot);

    if (visualization) {
        auto box = std::make_shared<ChBoxShape>();
        box->GetBoxGeometry().Size = size;
        box->GetBoxGeometry().Pos = pos;
        box->GetBoxGeometry().Rot = ChMatrix33<>(rot);
        body->GetAssets().push_back(box);
    }
}

(Note the lines in red, different from what is in AddBoxGeometry)

If you use other shapes, you'll need to write similar new utility functions (e.g., MyAddSphereGeometry).

I have not tested the above code.  Please let me know if this resolves your current problem.

--Radu


