Matt,

Note that this bug (and a few others) were fixed when I switched to using Eigen throughout Chrono.  You must be using an older version of the code.  If possible, I strongly suggest you switch to using the latest version in the 'develop' branch, especially if you're working on extending Chrono capabilities.

With the migration to Eigen, things have changed quite a bit under the hood.  In particular, the function you mentioned now looks like this:

void ChConstraintNgeneric::MultiplyTandAdd(ChVectorDynamic<double>& result, double l) {
    for (size_t i = 0; i < variables.size(); ++i) {
        if (variables[i]->IsActive()) {
            result.segment(variables[i]->GetOffset(), Cq[i].size()) += Cq[i].transpose() * l;
        }
    }
}

--Radu

