Subject: Re: [chrono] Anyway to unfixed top node in cables, after delay?
From: Radu Serban
Date: Mon, 17 Dec 2018 11:19:21 +0000

Justin,

This is a problem only because of the way that demo is set up (the "builder" goes out of scope at each loop iteration).

You can get around this issue by using multiple "builders" (of type ChBuilderBeamANCF) that persists until you want to access one of their nodes in order to release it.
Better yet, you can only maintain a vector of the nodes (from different cables) that you want to modify later on.  Something along the following lines:

std::vector<std::shared_ptr<ChNodeFEAxyzD>> top_nodes;
for (...) {
  ChBuilderBeamANCF builder;
  builder.BuildBeam(...);
  ...
  top_nodes.push_back(builder.GetLastBeamNodes().front());
  ...
}

and later on invoke SetFixed(false) on the nodes in top_nodes:

for (auto& node : top_nodes) {
  node->SetFixed(false);
}

Hope that this helps,
--Radu


