Subject: ChQuaternion::operator*= bugged
From: lucas.letournel@dice-engineering.com
Date: Wed, 7 Nov 2018 01:43:29 -0800 (PST)

Hello,

I just ran into something that seemed bugged to me, in the 
ChQuaternion::operator*=. I am still using Chrono with the commit 

934064d2ccf8e9690373a0fd03c93e91c7f4b2c8


The operator*= is based on the Cross method, applied to this : 

this->Cross(*this, other);


But in Cross, this.data is modified on one line, and used also for 
calculating the following ones.

For a quick check, you can try this :

chrono::ChQuaternion<double> First (1.,0.,0.,0.);
chrono::ChQuaternion<double> Second (0.7,0.7,0.,0.);

chrono::ChQuaternion<double> Result;
Result = First*Second;
std::cout<<"Result : e0 = "<<Result.e0()<<", e1 = "<<Result.e1()<<", e2 = "<<Result.e2()<<", e3 = "<<Result.e3()<<std::endl;

First *= Second;
std::cout<<"First  : e0 = "<<First.e0()<<", e1 = "<<First.e1()<<", e2 = "<<First.e2()<<", e3 = "<<First.e3()<<std::endl;


Result and First should be equals to Second, since First is the unit 
quaternion. While the operator* gives the right result, the operator*= 
gives a wrong one.

I think this bug was not spotted earlier since the compositions of 
rotations are done usually using rotation matrices in ChFrame.

Best regards,

Lucas Letournel

