From: Radu Serban
Date: Wed, 30 Jan 2019 07:46:15 +0000

Huck,

That's correct, with such an implementation the variable 'app' would not be defined outside the scope of the if block.

One option is to use conditional compilation, using a macro. But that would require recompiling the code whenever you want to enable/disable the run-time visualization.

Alternatively, use a pointer to a ChWheeledVehicleIrrApp:

ChWheeledVehicleIrrApp* app = nullptr;
if (gui) {
  app = new ChWheeledVehicleIrrApp(...);
  app->SetSkyBox();
  ...
  app->AssetBindAll();
  app->AssetUpdateAll();
}

...

if(gui) {
  app->BeginScene();
  app->DrawAll();
  ...
}

...
delete app;

--Radu


