Subject: Re: [chrono] Contact information in Parallel module
From: Radu Serban
Date: Wed, 10 May 2017 19:23:10 +0200

Scott,

You could directly access the data arrays in the "data manager" (a 
public member of ChSystemParallel), but that requires you to understand 
where/how data is stored there.

So I just implemented a missing piece in Chrono::Parallel, namely 
support for ChContactContainerParallel::ReportAllContacts().  With this, 
you provide a user-defined callback class (inherited from 
ChContactContainer::ReportContactCallback) which implements the 
OnReportContact method.   This method will be called once for each 
contact pair currently stored in the contact container.   Note that, in 
this current implementation, contact forces and torques are not reported 
(i.e., you will always get zero vectors for those); but all other 
geometric contact information should be available.

I pushed this change to the Chrono repository.  This means that you 
would also need to update your code to reflect the API changes I made a 
few days ago.

To use this feature, you need to do something like this:

class MyReporter : public ChContactContainer::ReportContactCallback {
public:
    virtual bool OnReportContact(...) {
          // process/report/output this contact
          return true;
    }
};

int main() {
    ChSystemParallelNSC system;
    ...
    MyReporter reporter;
    ...
    while (...) {
         system.DoStepDynamics(time_step);
system.GetContactContainer()->ReportAllContacts(&reporter);
    }
}

Hope that this helps,
--Radu

