contact you're interested in and/or perform any actions you want.

Once you have this user-defined class, you can invoke it at any time 
during the simulation loop, using something like:

class MyReporter : public ChContactContainer::ReportContactCallback {
public:
  MyReporter(...) {...}
  virtual bool OnReportContact(...) {...}
};

ChSystemNSC my_system;
MyReporter my_reporter(...);

while (...) {
  ...
  my_system.DoStepDynamics(step_size);
my_system.GetContactContainer()->ReportAllContacts(&my_reporter);
  ...
}

A couple more comments:

  * If you are interested in grabbing information for only one
    particular contact, as soon as you found it return 'false' from
    OnReportContact to stop contact scanning (in case there are many
    others that you don't care about)
  * You mention "spheres of small radius". Beware of "tunneling
    effects" where collision involving fast-moving small objects may be
    missed altogether. Make sure your integration step size is small
    enough.

Hope that this helps,
