Subject: Re: Cohesion not working?!
From: Morten Haastrup
Date: Thu, 20 Aug 2015 08:23:54 -0700 (PDT)

Hi Ben

I spent a lot of time playing around with the cohesion and figured out that 
you have to set it each time a contact is calculated. And if you want to 
use compliance different from zero you have to set that each time as well 
(only when using cohesion). This is implemented  in this way:

class MyContactCallback : public ChSystem::ChCustomCollisionPointCallback
{
public: 
    void ContactCallback(const collision::ChCollisionInfo& mcontactinfo, 
ChMaterialCouple&  material) ///< get info about contact (cannot change it))
    {
        double t = mySystem->GetChTime();
        double step = mySystem->GetStep();
        material.compliance = Compliance;
        material.complianceT = Compliance;
        material.cohesion = (float)(step * Cohesion);
    }
public:
    MyContactCallback(float cohesion){ this->Cohesion = cohesion; };
    void SetCohesion(float cohesion){ this->Cohesion = cohesion; };
    void SetCompliance(float Compliance){ this->Compliance = Compliance; };
    void SetSystem(ChSystem *mySystem){ this->mySystem = mySystem; };
private:
    float Cohesion;
    float Compliance;
    ChSystem *mySystem;
};
And then you have to add these lines somewhere in your main function:
MyContactCallback *myCall = (new MyContactCallback((float)Cohesion));
myCall->SetCompliance((float)Compliance);
myCall->SetSystem(&mySystem);
mySystem.SetCustomCollisionPointCallback(myCall);

I don't know if you already know this, but I hope it helps.
Cheers, Morten


