You want to define a prismatic joint "in a generic direction."
Being more precise, you want the z-axis of the rotation part of the
ChCoordsys passed into the link Initialize() function pointing in a
specific direction. So check that your rotation satisfies that:

 ChQuaternion<> test_q(0.0600032, 0.455768, -0.540625, 0.704556);
  ChVector<> test_z = test_q.GetZaxis();
  GetLog() << " Z AXIS !!! : " << test_z;

That Z-axis from the csys rotation needs to point in the direction of your
translational DOF. It should point from A to B, so something like:
  ChVector<> pt_B(10, 0, 10);
  ChVector<> pt_A(0, 10, 0);
  ChVector<> z_from_pts(pt_B - pt_A);
  z_from_pts.Normalize();
  GetLog() << " Z Axis from point location: " << z_from_pts;\

There's your problem.

Justin

