Subject: Re: [chrono] Creation of bodies
From: Radu Serban
Date: Tue, 19 Jun 2018 21:06:19 +0200

Hi Davide,

You can create a body at any time inside your simulation loop. Just make 
sure to add it to the system and, if using Irrlicht, to bind its 
visualization assets to the Irrlicht 'application'. Something along the 
following lines:

bool created = false;
...
while (t < t_end) {
  if (!created && t >= 10) {
  auto new_body = std::shared_ptr<ChBody>(my_system.NewBody());
  new_body->SetMass(...);
  ...
  my_system.AddBody(new_body);

  my_app.AssetBind(new_body);
  my_app.AssetUpdate(new_body);

  created = true;
  }
  ...
  my_system.DoStepDynamics(step_size);
  ...
  t += step_size;
}

You can see something similar in various demos; for example 
demo_IRR_conveyor or demo_VEH_HMMWV_Parallel (the latter is a 
Chrono::Parallel example in which an entire vehicle is created at a time 
after the start of the simulation).

Since Chrono only implements one-step integration methods, you can also 
change the step size at any time before a call to DoStepDynamics.

--Radu


