This condition is enforced for the default collision system (in an indirect way; see lines 404-408 in ChBroadphaseUtils.h).  I have not worked on the Bullet-based collision system in Chrono::Parallel, but it appears that there is no provision there for enforcing this condition.

I have only a couple of simple tests I can use to check for issues when using Bullet and I was not able to reproduce this issue;  of course, this is not to say it doesn't exist, as you seem to have hit it.   If you happen to have a simple example that shows this problem, it'd be great if you could share that with me.

Having said that, I was wondering if you could try the following fix.  In the implementation of ReportContacts (file ChCollisionSystemBulletParallel.cpp) insert the code in red below right after line 148:

  btPersistentManifold* contactManifold = bt_collision_world->getDispatcher()->getManifoldByIndexInternal(i);
  btCollisionObject* obA = static_cast<btCollisionObject*>(contactManifold->getBody0());
  btCollisionObject* obB = static_cast<btCollisionObject*>(contactManifold->getBody1());
  if (obB->getCompanionId() < obA->getCompanionId()) {
      auto tmp = obA;
      obA = obB;
      obB = tmp;
  }
  contactManifold->refreshContactPoints(obA->getWorldTransform(), obB->getWorldTransform());

Please let me know if this fixes the problem and I will push the change to the Github repo.

Best,
